{"title":"Discriminant","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>discriminant</b> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation\" title=\"Quadratic equation\">quadratic equation</a> of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/6/176e39482753e1e116cf3e6bae7715f0e51858a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a{x}^2+b{x}+{c}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" /> is the quantity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b583c5da82fc9dfee108cfc8bd890a63051a9dbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2-4ac$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"64\" height=\"15\" />.  When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/8787d75d65f6e66e472a00969f027ae739b4b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${a},{b},{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> are real, this is a notable quantity, because if the discriminant is positive, the equation has two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Real\">real</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Root\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Root\">roots</a>; if the discriminant is negative, the equation has two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nonreal\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Nonreal\">nonreal</a> roots; and if the discriminant is 0, the equation has a real <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Double_root\" title=\"Double root\">double root</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Discriminant_of_polynomials_of_degree_n\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Discriminant of polynomials of degree n</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#General_formula_of_discriminant\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">General formula of discriminant</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#When\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">When</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#When_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">When</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#When_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">When</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Some_properties\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Some properties</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Example_Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Example Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Introductory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Other_resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Other resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Discriminant_of_polynomials_of_degree_n\">Discriminant of polynomials of degree n</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Discriminant of polynomials of degree n\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The discriminant can tell us something about the roots of a given <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial\" title=\"Polynomial\">polynomial</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/8/8289f0b7244af65263af3fafa01f634af6e3e87f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)=a_nx^n+a_{n-1}x^{n-1}+...+a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"266\" height=\"19\" /> of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> with all the coefficients being real. But for polynomials of degree 4 or higher it can be difficult to use it.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"General_formula_of_discriminant\">General formula of discriminant</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: General formula of discriminant\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We know that the discriminant of a polynomial is the product of the squares of the differences of the polynomial roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c42077f2a447ca548cdbfe63f1932e9866df3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, so,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/4/df4e5a18f9ce3f0f9ab0ecac74d2dc4b34ce3b47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D(p)=a_n^{2n-2}\\prod_{i&lt;j}^{n}(r_i-r_j)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"202\" height=\"50\" />\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"When\">When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: When\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>Given a polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81ad057aedfeded836ee205a34803a6c23e999a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)=ax^2+bx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"19\" />, its discriminant is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/4/144698dbdeff4bbfcd9c01b2d89a699bbfb7e81b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D(p)=b^2-4ac$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"19\" />, which can also be denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/e/c5e45f290267432d6b5202adb894a75bf362b1e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta=b^2-4ac$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/1/e210e6ea59a93633f7271e3290dc0abfd1372108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> we have the graph\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Delta_greater_than_0.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ac/Delta_greater_than_0.png/261px-Delta_greater_than_0.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"261\" height=\"300\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ac/Delta_greater_than_0.png/391px-Delta_greater_than_0.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ac/Delta_greater_than_0.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>which has two distinct real roots.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/9/b99da3f6c3627b98d86ebc1a10e5b032e94a961a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> we have the graph\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Delta_lower_than_0.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/6e/Delta_lower_than_0.png/261px-Delta_lower_than_0.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"261\" height=\"300\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/6/6e/Delta_lower_than_0.png/391px-Delta_lower_than_0.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/6/6e/Delta_lower_than_0.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>which has two non-real roots.\n</p><p>And for the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c05735937ca1e89d4dde9237851fb5bc92ed93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta=0$\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />,\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Delta_equal_to_0.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/5f/Delta_equal_to_0.png/300px-Delta_equal_to_0.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"282\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/5f/Delta_equal_to_0.png 1.5x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"When_2\">When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: When\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>The discriminant of a polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea27e84f127657b724a1a2943275b62fe782334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)=ax^3+bx^2+cx+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"206\" height=\"19\" /> is given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/1/8c15052565a27c1c624c4cca2ffe06f59fb6e52f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D(p)=b^2c^2-4b^3d-4ac^3+18abcd-27a^2d^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"354\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nAlso, the depressed <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cubic_Equation\" title=\"Cubic Equation\">cubic</a> form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb705dcdbc557cf407925c691391531dd37369bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(z)=z^3+pz+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"19\" /> has discriminant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/5/60531a9351d9112a5fb0d3a1e75e4a2bc8a0b6a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D(p)=-4p^3-27q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"19\" />. We can compress a polynomial of degree 3, which also makes possible to us to use Cardano's formula, by doing the substitution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/6/6b6f309eacedc34b7d2bcdc4dfd4acdbad7db324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=z-\\frac{a}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"78\" height=\"33\" /> on the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/501f6a0c1db07a1436d5448d4fa4499ef53ad122.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)=x^3+ax^2+bx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f92f2b19827ba2b3e6f39e36a629d25cad9ad8e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=0$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, then at least two of the roots are equal;</li></ul>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Cubic_delta%3D0_01.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f5/Cubic_delta%3D0_01.png/600px-Cubic_delta%3D0_01.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"310\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f5/Cubic_delta%3D0_01.png/900px-Cubic_delta%3D0_01.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f5/Cubic_delta%3D0_01.png/1200px-Cubic_delta%3D0_01.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Cubic_delta%3D0_02.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/41/Cubic_delta%3D0_02.png/600px-Cubic_delta%3D0_02.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"310\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/41/Cubic_delta%3D0_02.png/900px-Cubic_delta%3D0_02.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/41/Cubic_delta%3D0_02.png/1200px-Cubic_delta%3D0_02.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/7/b07c0a3b341aaf7325cee276d623abded580231e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />, then all three roots are real and distinct;</li></ul>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Cubic_delta_less_0.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/70/Cubic_delta_less_0.png/600px-Cubic_delta_less_0.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"309\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/70/Cubic_delta_less_0.png/900px-Cubic_delta_less_0.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/70/Cubic_delta_less_0.png/1200px-Cubic_delta_less_0.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4cc61c52a21cc54723c9a8acd11ce2e2b90ec551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />, then one of the roots is real and the other two are complex conjugate.</li></ul>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Cubic_delta_greater_0.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/31/Cubic_delta_greater_0.png/600px-Cubic_delta_greater_0.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"310\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/31/Cubic_delta_greater_0.png/900px-Cubic_delta_greater_0.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/31/Cubic_delta_greater_0.png/1200px-Cubic_delta_greater_0.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"When_3\">When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cf3e35a4981583288d2a7c4b34989916fb7360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: When\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quartic_Equation\" title=\"Quartic Equation\">quartic polynomial</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49bf0859c47c73bd60d22d6d6d6de2ba81391c73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)=ax^4+bx^3+cx^2+dx+e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"254\" height=\"19\" /> has discriminant\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fc28aa2cf412b2afd9c600d8b8c3475b9298367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D(p)=256a^3e^3-192a^2bde^2-128a^2c^2e^2+144a^2cd^2e-27a^2d^4+144ab^2ce^2-6ab^2d^2e-80abc^2de+18abcd^3+16ac^4e-4ac^3d^2-27b^4e^2+18b^3cde-4b^3d^3-4b^2c^3e+b^2c^2d^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"1049\" height=\"36\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f92f2b19827ba2b3e6f39e36a629d25cad9ad8e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=0$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, then at least two of the roots are equal;</li>\n<li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4cc61c52a21cc54723c9a8acd11ce2e2b90ec551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />, then the roots are all real or all non-real;</li>\n<li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/7/b07c0a3b341aaf7325cee276d623abded580231e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />, then there are two real roots and two complex conjugate roots.</li></ul>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Some_properties\">Some properties</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Some properties\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e17604827a9e0609eeea40c2fa99c2cff1afd1f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> we can say that\n</p>\n<ul><li>The polynomial has a multiple root if, and only if, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f92f2b19827ba2b3e6f39e36a629d25cad9ad8e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=0$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />;</li>\n<li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/c/4cc61c52a21cc54723c9a8acd11ce2e2b90ec551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> being a positive integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1c3beccf3fc0106bdbd157f6eedba33097ce5fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq\\frac{n}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"33\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> being the degree of the polynomial, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea7ee8a282949fd853a01537ec7a2b55e56f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> pairs of complex conjugate roots  and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/787ac5437ed73fcd70ecc6445641fc0a37ebeb9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-4k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> real roots;</li>\n<li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/7/b07c0a3b341aaf7325cee276d623abded580231e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> being a positive integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/6582a8cd9e0c666b88ca777b55978c67ba59575e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq\\frac{n-2}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />, then there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f2789508227865dfc89fd46e18ae9b25bff34257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> pairs of complex conjugate roots and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf46932b323368183cfaebcdf0230e9f50ca38f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-4k+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> real roots.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Example_Problems\">Example Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Example Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>(AMC 12 2005) There are two values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> for which the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2368ad196f742e537edba04863d1c4816249c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^2+ax+8x+9=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"175\" height=\"16\" /> has only one solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. What is the sum of these values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />?</li></ul>\n<p>Solution: Since we want the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />'s where there is only one solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, the discriminant has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b67372f665481c4d0be90ca098ad62fe52ecc2f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+8)^2-4(4)(9)=a^2+16a-80=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"304\" height=\"19\" />. The sum of these values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/09372266f72fa589bc1aba24cf2c6e85c55d946b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1977 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1\"> 1977 Canadian MO Problem 1</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Other_resources\">Other resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Other resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discriminant\">Wikipedia entry</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202127\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.062 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.147 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 305/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9998/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1687:|#|:idhash:cano